{"cluster_id": "C-0578", "topic": "CAS correctness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B003-115"], "canonical_claim": "A live committed manifest ref structurally protects its referenced blobs from GC because the fold cannot mark them zero-in-degree, and deletion additionally waits through condemn and `delete_pending`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/09-read-protocol.md#gc-safety"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0579", "topic": "CAS correctness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B003-121"], "canonical_claim": "The current CAS safety model assumes one-live-object semantics; versioned-bucket marker stacks and version-specific conditional behavior are unmodeled.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/10-backups.md#no-versioning-stack"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0580", "topic": "CAS correctness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B004-019"], "canonical_claim": "The CAS safety triad is no-dangle, no-loss, and no-return: live references resolve through present keys, deletion requires durable retirement and later zero reachability with the exact token, and a retired `(kind, hash, token)` cannot become a valid dependency again.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/11-walkthrough.md#safety-invariants"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0581", "topic": "CAS correctness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B004-024"], "canonical_claim": "An operation with an uncertain conditional-write outcome is treated as `PrecommitState::Uncertain`, which behaves as `NotAttempted` for admission and as `Durable` for cleanup.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/11-walkthrough.md#safety-invariants"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0582", "topic": "CAS correctness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B004-028", "B004-053", "B004-084"], "canonical_claim": "`writer_epoch` is durable-monotone and never reissued, and every re-materialization of a fixed `(namespace, shard)` carries a strictly greater incarnation to close ABA. Additionally, `writer_epoch` is durably monotone, while `build_sequence` resets on process start; global ordering is the lexicographic pair `(writer_epoch, build_sequence)`. Additionally, The planned shard incarnation is the existing `(writer_epoch, build_sequence)` pair, represented as `ShardIncarnation`, with `{0,0}` meaning unstamped; a recreated `(ns, shard)` must receive a strictly greater pair under `INC-MONO`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/11-walkthrough.md#counters", "docs/superpowers/cas/11-walkthrough.md#safety-invariants", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-01-cas-shard-incarnation-and-registry-removal.md#L14-L28"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0583", "topic": "CAS correctness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B004-031"], "canonical_claim": "CAS crash safety is intentionally asymmetric: every crash point may leak objects, but no crash point loses acknowledged data or creates a dangling reference.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/11-walkthrough.md#durability-claims"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0584", "topic": "CAS correctness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B004-046"], "canonical_claim": "A writer that adopts a blob token must have observed a non-`Condemned` marker after its precommit edge became durable, so the next GC fold can spare the blob; a resurrection changes the token and makes a stale `deleteExact` return `TokenMismatch`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/11-walkthrough.md#writer-gc-race"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0585", "topic": "CAS correctness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B004-091", "B004-109"], "canonical_claim": "The planned ref-shard reclaim is fail-closed on a concurrent revive: an append changes the token, `deleteExact` returns `TokenMismatch`, and the shard survives with its new content. Additionally, A revive append after a shard tombstone changes the object token, so `deleteExact` returns `TokenMismatch` and the shard survives; an idle-but-live empty shard without a tombstone is retained.", "issue_ids": ["D1"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-01-cas-shard-incarnation-and-registry-removal.md#L253-L292", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-01-cas-shard-incarnation-and-registry-removal-design.md#reclaim"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0586", "topic": "CAS correctness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B004-111"], "canonical_claim": "D1 requires `THM-NO-RETURN`, `INV-NO-DANGLING`, `INV-NO-ABA`, and `INV-NO-BLOB-LEAK`; the last requires every `-1` edge to be folded before its carrying shard is deleted.", "issue_ids": ["D1"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-01-cas-shard-incarnation-and-registry-removal-design.md#invariants"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0587", "topic": "CAS correctness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B004-122"], "canonical_claim": "Copy-forward verification requires a valid envelope, matching object kind, and recomputed logical hash equal to the key hash; any mismatch or 404 is fail-closed, with corruption reported as `CORRUPTED_DATA` and a lost-race 404 as `ABORTED`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-02-cas-copy-forward-condemned-evidence.md#L128-L135", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-02-cas-copy-forward-condemned-evidence.md#L36-L59"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0588", "topic": "CAS correctness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B004-126"], "canonical_claim": "`CaGcAckFloorCore` models copy-forward as minting and binding a fresh incarnation only while the blob is present and the current token is visible in the writer's loaded retired view; there is no absent-source copy-forward arm.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-02-cas-copy-forward-condemned-evidence.md#L69-L81"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0589", "topic": "CAS correctness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B004-142"], "canonical_claim": "The ack-floor redesign rejects old schema versions fail-closed: schema versions are bumped, malformed data yields `CORRUPTED_DATA`, and future versions yield `NOT_IMPLEMENTED`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-02-cas-gc-ack-floor-fence.md#L18-L37"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0590", "topic": "CAS correctness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B005-012"], "canonical_claim": "A GC pass must durably write retired-list and snapshot runs before the `gc/state` CAS that publishes `round := K`, so any reader observing round K can load retired-list version K.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-02-cas-gc-ack-floor-fence-redesign.md#gcstate"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0591", "topic": "CAS correctness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B005-014"], "canonical_claim": "A mounted writer acknowledges a GC round only after it has loaded that round's retired list, drained all old-view `mutateShard` calls, and installed the new view; the advertised `observed_gc_round` never exceeds the installed and drained view.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-02-cas-gc-ack-floor-fence-redesign.md#writer-protocol"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0592", "topic": "CAS correctness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B005-021"], "canonical_claim": "GC fence-outs complete before discovery and their writers' last commits are therefore durable before the sweep begins.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-02-cas-gc-ack-floor-fence-redesign.md#gc-round-protocol-one-pass"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0593", "topic": "CAS correctness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B005-034"], "canonical_claim": "A delete at pass K is safe because a writer with view `V \u2265 condemn_round` sees the retired token and recreates it, while a writer with `V < condemn_round` must have been terminated or fenced out before the sweep and its commits are folded into the same merge.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-02-cas-gc-ack-floor-fence-redesign.md#safety-argument"]}
