{"cluster_id": "C-0595", "topic": "CAS correctness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B005-077"], "canonical_claim": "If `snap_generation > 0` but the adopted fold seal, a referenced run, or a referenced retired object is absent or corrupt, GC must throw `CORRUPTED_DATA` rather than treating the artifact as an empty baseline.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-03-cas-gc-rebuild-design.md#part-1--the-guard-fail-closed-independent-ships-first"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0596", "topic": "CAS correctness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B005-079"], "canonical_claim": "The rebuild is live-conservative: events after a shard read remain above the recorded cursor for the next regular round, a live precommit with an absent body clamps the cursor below its transition, and new condemnations wait for mount acknowledgements past the rebuilt round.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-03-cas-gc-rebuild-design.md#L47-L56"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0597", "topic": "CAS correctness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B005-104", "B005-105"], "canonical_claim": "The GCS dialect throws `LOGICAL_ERROR` for an `If-None-Match` value other than `*` and for a non-numeric `If-Match` value, rather than silently changing conditional semantics. Additionally, The GCS dialect throws `LOGICAL_ERROR` before sending a conditional `CompleteMultipartUpload`, identified as POST with an `uploadId` query parameter and no `partNumber`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-03-cas-gcs-generation-binding-design.md#the-conditional-dialect--shared-helper-in-pocohttpclienthcpp"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0598", "topic": "CAS correctness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B006-008"], "canonical_claim": "Before applying each queued closure, the leader snapshots the in-memory `RootShard`; if the closure throws, the snapshot is restored, that promise receives the exception, and the remaining batch items continue.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-03-cas-shard-mutation-queue.md#L68-L70"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0599", "topic": "CAS correctness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B006-068"], "canonical_claim": "The load-bearing GC safety invariant is: no destructive decision is ever made on a not-fully-folded snapshot; any pending-delete graduation forces a FOLD before deletion so a protective `+1` is observed.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-06-cas-gc-round-skip-unchanged-design.md#L97-L118"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0600", "topic": "CAS correctness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B006-073"], "canonical_claim": "The required `CaGcRoundDeferCore` TLA+ gate must establish `NoOverDelete` and `EventuallyFolded`; sabotage allowing graduation on a stale snapshot must produce a `NoOverDelete` counterexample, and sabotage removing the defer bound must produce an `EventuallyFolded` counterexample.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-06-cas-gc-round-skip-unchanged-design.md#L181-L202"]}
